From e2d7225666acf711ffaddb9a4fa438f2f13cf5e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AegisOS Build <build@aegisos.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 01:48:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 75/85] aegisos: redeem the active-dismiss grant proactively
 instead of on a gesture

The authorized branch of handleUserSwitchComplete already skips the
automatic bouncer re-arm, but did nothing else: the device was left
showing a swipeable lock screen until the user's own next gesture
happened to request a bouncer, which is the one place the third
(active-dismiss) grant from the same mint gets redeemed. An ordinary,
same-user unlock (confirmed against this exact build: PIN typed into
an already-showing bouncer) never shows this intermediate lock screen
at all, so the swipe is a real, hardware-confirmed tell (ADR-085),
not stock behavior to leave alone.

Proactively calls the same dismiss() the unauthorized branch already
uses, on the same 500ms delay, redeeming the still-outstanding grant
immediately instead of leaving it to chance. This is unvalidated on
hardware: the mechanism is traced through source (dismissAndCollapse
-> executeRunnableDismissingKeyguard -> dismissKeyguardThenExecute ->
PrimaryBouncerInteractor#show -> showNextSecurityScreenOrFinish, the
same active-dismiss chokepoint a real user gesture already redeems
correctly today), but the existing test this change updates asserted
the opposite behavior deliberately, so this needs a real touch-input
hardware trial -- not just a passing unit test -- before it is treated
as confirmed, matching the same rigor Tasks 11a-11c already required
for this class of change.
---
 .../keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java        | 31 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
index dbf5383599b8..303977013de5 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/keyguard/KeyguardViewMediator.java
@@ -782,12 +782,31 @@ public class KeyguardViewMediator implements CoreStartable,
             // holds a still-valid, not-yet-consumed authorization for exactly this purpose;
             // every other secure-user switch (including any switch this authorization was never
             // minted for) is unaffected and still re-arms the bouncer as before.
-            if (mLockPatternUtils.isSecure(userId)
-                    && !mLockPatternUtils.consumeDecoySwitchAuthorizationForBouncerSkip(userId)) {
-                // We are calling dismiss with a delay as there are race conditions in some
-                // scenarios caused by async layout listeners
-                mHandler.postDelayed(
-                        () -> dismiss(null /* callback */, null /* message */), mDismissToken, 500);
+            if (mLockPatternUtils.isSecure(userId)) {
+                if (!mLockPatternUtils.consumeDecoySwitchAuthorizationForBouncerSkip(userId)) {
+                    // We are calling dismiss with a delay as there are race conditions in some
+                    // scenarios caused by async layout listeners
+                    mHandler.postDelayed(
+                            () -> dismiss(null /* callback */, null /* message */), mDismissToken,
+                            500);
+                } else {
+                    // AegisOS: the automatic re-arm above was just skipped because this switch
+                    // was authorized, but nothing else drives the keyguard forward from here --
+                    // left alone, the device sits on a swipeable lock screen until the user's own
+                    // next gesture happens to request a bouncer, which is the one place the third
+                    // (active-dismiss) grant from the same mint gets redeemed (see
+                    // UserController#consumeDecoySwitchAuthorizationForActiveDismiss).
+                    // Proactively requesting the same dismiss here, on the same delay, redeems
+                    // that still-outstanding grant immediately instead of leaving it to a
+                    // gesture: it goes through the identical showNextSecurityScreenOrFinish()
+                    // chokepoint trust-agent and biometric dismissals already use, gated on the
+                    // same single-use, credential-verified authorization this exact switch
+                    // already earned -- not a new dismiss authority, just triggering the existing
+                    // one proactively.
+                    mHandler.postDelayed(
+                            () -> dismiss(null /* callback */, null /* message */), mDismissToken,
+                            500);
+                }
             }
         }
         // We need to adjust the status bar in case there are race conditions where the
